Z||000003||HF6582||05-10-99||05:26 PM||||the stock internals of a 2.8L are supposed<br>to be good to 7000rpm. A 3.1L uses the same<br>rods, it is the crank and piston compression<br>height that make the differance in displacement. the rods are considered to <br>be the weak link in the motor, so if the rods<br>can take the rpm the rest of the motor should.
